Package: cap
Version: 4.1-RELEASE
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: bash (>= 4.0), coreutils, util-linux, rsync
Recommends: pdsh, shellcheck
Installed-Size: 3300
Maintainer: cdmaestas <cdmaestas@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/cdmaestas/cap
Description: Cluster Administration Package (build/install framework)
 CAP5 is a build/install framework (deploy, cfunc, and packaging
 pipeline) originally built to bundle and deploy common HPC cluster
 tools (pdsh, genders, slurm, munge, conman, freeipmi, powerman, and
 more) through a single interface.
 .
 Project status: preserved, not revived. The framework itself is
 maintained and works today. The tool recipes under src/ are a
 historical snapshot from 2012; most of their download URLs point at
 hosts that no longer exist. See src/README.md in the source
 distribution for details.
